## 2026-09-27 (topic recording mode)

Marty asked where topic discovery lives, and for a mode where the
subscriber records topics continuously so a later query reports
everything seen since start rather than only what is there at that
instant.

Where it lives: split across both, on purpose. The transport and the
callbacks are on `PureJavaZenohSubscriber`, because discovery rides
the same session as ordinary subscribing and there is nothing to
connect separately. The state is in `TopicRegistry` / `TopicInfo` /
`TopicSource`, which are their own classes in the same package so the
registry mutators can stay package-private. Contrast with
`PureJavaZenohScout`, which IS a separate top-level class, because it
speaks UDP multicast and never opens a session at all.

Added a cumulative mode to `TopicRegistry`, chosen at construction:
- Live (default, what was there before): a topic drops out once its
  last declaration is withdrawn.
- Cumulative: nothing is ever removed; departed topics stay with
  `active()` false.
Observed traffic remains sticky in both, on the grounds that a message
really having arrived is not something a later event can retract.

`TopicInfo` changed shape to carry the distinction. `sources()` is now
cumulative over the entry's lifetime and never shrinks;
`activeSources()` is the subset still standing; `active()` is
`!activeSources().isEmpty()`. Added `TopicInfo.active(...)` as a
factory for the all-current case. Also stopped `recordUndeclaration`
advancing `lastSeenMs`: a withdrawal is negative evidence, so on an
inactive topic the field now answers "when was it last really there".

Subscriber additions:
- Builder: `recordTopics(boolean)` (default false),
  `recordTopicsPattern(String)` (default `**`),
  `recordTopicTraffic(boolean)` (default true).
- `start()` opens the recorder when the flag is set. Deliberately NOT
  fatal on failure: a router can allow the session and refuse the
  discovery interest or the wildcard subscription, and that must not
  stop the caller subscribing to the keys they came for. Logs WARNING
  and carries on.
- `startRecordingTopics()` / `stopRecordingTopics()` /
  `isRecordingTopics()` / `topicRegistry()` / `recordedTopics()`.
- `stop()` closes the recorder FIRST, so its FINAL interest goes out
  while the session is still open.
- New 3-arg `topics(pattern, observeTraffic, cumulative)`; the 2-arg
  form delegates with cumulative=false, so existing behaviour is
  unchanged.

`recordedTopics()` throws IllegalStateException when recording was
never started, rather than returning an empty list. An empty list is
indistinguishable from "found nothing", which is precisely the wrong
answer to give for a discovery API whose whole documented weakness is
that absence proves nothing.

Tests 82 to 90 (8 new in `TopicRegistryTest` covering cumulative
retention, activeOnly, partial withdrawal, and the lastSeenMs rule).
All green. Javadoc with the workflow's exact flag set is exit 0.
README and API.md updated, including the subscriber builder table.

