  sample package was renamed to `sample.zenoh`). javadoc exits 2 with
  "No source files for package io.mdudel.zenoh.purejava" before doing
  any work, hence the near-instant failure. Nothing was wrong with the
  runner, the JDK setup, the Pages configuration, or the deploy step.
- Fixed: `-sourcepath src/main/java` and
  `-subpackages io.mdudel.zenoh.purejava:sample.zenoh`. Also replaced
  the stale header comment (it described the NetBeans Ant harness and
  its IDE-supplied `${platform.active}` property) and the stale
  `nbproject/project.properties` encoding reference with the Maven
  equivalents, and added a reminder to keep these paths in sync if
  packages move again.
- Verified locally with JDK 21 rather than by hand-reading: the OLD
  arguments reproduce the exact CI error and exit 2, the NEW arguments
  exit 0 and emit a complete doc tree. Remaining output is only
  pre-existing non-fatal warnings (unresolved `@link` targets, and raw
